IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-66. NOUNS of the four things this row records (items I1 to I4) about the Courts (Fees) Regulations, 5767-2007 (called "the Fees Regulations" in this row): a cited rule and the range that cancels it, a power cited by a subsection number, a figure printed twice, and the order of dated instruments.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: what the sources do not answer is not asked.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Fees Regulations. It records four things, as typed values the tests check, and keeps each defect as an expected-red test.
-- The names of the fields below are mine, not the Regulations'. The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module: `src:` lines are the consolidations (excerpts, deposited), `ext:[...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument.
-- A reading whose two sides differ is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.

§ `Nouns of a reading`

-- Where a reading comes from, from the stronger to the weaker.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
    `the consolidation only`

§ `Nouns of a cited rule (I1)`

-- A rule as the citing words print it ("143", or 214 with a letter after it) and the number the row compares with a range (the base number: the letter is not a number).
DECLARE `A cited rule` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the rule as the citing words print it` IS A STRING
    `the base number of the rule` IS A NUMBER
    `the instrument the citing words name` IS A STRING
    `the citing words were read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

-- A range of regulation numbers, as a cancelling regulation prints it.
DECLARE `A range of regulation numbers` HAS
    `the range as the cancelling words print it` IS A STRING
    `the first number of the range` IS A NUMBER
    `the last number of the range` IS A NUMBER
    `the regulation that prints the range` IS A STRING
    `the range was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

-- A saving clause, recorded as two flags: what the clause says about earlier proceedings, and whether it is qualified.
DECLARE `A saving clause` HAS
    `the regulation that prints the saving clause` IS A STRING
    `the earlier regulations continue for proceedings opened before the commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the continuation is qualified by a rule of the new regulations on which proceedings they apply to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the saving clause was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

-- A commencement day, as one reading of it: the Hebrew date as printed, the Gregorian date as printed, and the day the Hebrew-calendar routine gives for the Hebrew date. The row records two readings side by side and states no commencement day of its own.
DECLARE `A commencement reading` HAS
    `which reading this is` IS A STRING
    `where the reading was printed` IS A STRING
    `the Hebrew date printed` IS A STRING
    `the Gregorian date printed` IS A DATE
    `the day the Hebrew date falls on, by the routine` IS A DATE
    `the reading was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

-- A rule of the new Regulations as the page prints it: the number, the margin note and what the rule says. The row records what is printed and does not compare it with anything else.
DECLARE `A rule as a regulation prints it` HAS
    `the regulation and its page` IS A STRING
    `the number of the rule as printed` IS A NUMBER
    `the margin note, in English` IS A STRING
    `what the rule says, in English` IS A STRING
    `the printed rule was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a power citation (I2)`

DECLARE `A power citation` HAS
    `the opening words are in` IS A STRING
    `the section cited` IS A NUMBER
    `the citing words give a subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the subsection cited, as written` IS A STRING
    `the section is printed by the consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the subsection labels the consolidation prints in the section` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the opening words were read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `the target was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a threshold printed in an item (I3)`

DECLARE `A threshold printed in an item` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the notice and its page` IS A STRING
    `the figure printed beside the word that opens the threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `the first rate printed, in percent` IS A NUMBER
    `the second rate printed, in percent` IS A NUMBER
    `the threshold was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of dated instruments (I4)`

-- An item printed in an annual notice of the sums of a schedule.
DECLARE `An item printed in a notice` HAS
    `the item number` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount printed beside the item` IS A NUMBER
    `the notice was signed on` IS A DATE
    `the notice was published on` IS A DATE
    `the item is the item that regulation 4(3) of the 2017 temporary regulations adds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the item row was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

-- A regulation that says, for a period, that provisions of an earlier regulation are treated as cancelled.
DECLARE `A suspension` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A STRING
    `the suspension was signed on` IS A DATE
    `the suspension was published on` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
    `the first day the row takes for the period` IS A DATE
    `regulation 1 of the 2017 temporary regulations is treated as cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paragraph (3) of regulation 4 of the 2017 temporary regulations is treated as cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the suspension was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
